place: SERVICE_PENDING, under the `// s1-ws-wire (wave 3)` comment, after "projectFs/localPage/origin",
add: "projectFs/localPage/virtual",
# s1-ws-wire removes it when it registers the method: it is a new row with no service yet.

file: native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace/src/service.rs (task s1-ws-wire)
place: the projectFs/localPage handlers (next to projectFs/localPage/origin)
add: handler for "projectFs/localPage/virtual": decode the params' files into `pageserver::virtual_pages::VirtualFileInput { path, data_base64, text, content_type: type }`,
     `let files = virtual_pages::build_files(inputs)?;` (an invalid file list is an InvalidParams error), then
     `let url = page_server.lease_virtual(files, params.owner_id).await?;` and answer `{ "url": url }`.
     The PageAuthority the service mounts must answer Ok for `PageScope::Virtual { .. }`: the lease is the caller's own content, there is no
     grant or folder to check (the old desktop passed `authorize: async () => {}` or the owner-open check; a closed owner is handled by
     revoke_owner, which the existing projectFs/localPage/revokeOwner already calls).
     A `match` on `PageScope` anywhere else (none today outside pageserver/serve.rs) needs the `Virtual` arm.
